From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Michael C. Ferguson" <michael.christopher.ferguson@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: socfpga: de10nano: describe the MiSTer HPS<->FPGA
 interface

Describe every fixed HPS<->FPGA resource the board has, as one tree:

  /reserved-memory   no-map tiles covering 0x1ff00000..0x3fffffff: the
                     DDR above mem=511M, the U-Boot handoff page, the ascal
                     scaler, the HPS framebuffer (MiSTer_fb gains a
                     memory-region phandle) and the core-owned remainder.
  /mister            map-only generic-uio windows: the LW bridge, the heavy
                     HPS-to-FPGA bridge, the FPGA-manager page (GPO/GPI),
                     the 512 MiB DDR aperture (write-combined with 0045) and
                     the low DDR window.
  /mister/fabric-irqs
                     one generic-uio node per f2h_irq line 1..63 (GIC SPI
                     41..103). Line 0 stays MiSTer_fb's vsync.

Supersedes the beta-only 0043 (doorbells) and 0044 (LW window, DDR
aperture). Their UIO names are kept: mister_doorbell1..8 (lines 8..15),
mister_lw_window, mister_ddr_aperture. Additive: stock Main_MiSTer uses
/dev/mem and sees no change; under mem=511M the carve-outs lie outside
memblock.memory, so no mapping attribute moves.

Appended as a second root block so it merges into MiSTer_fb and
/reserved-memory without touching them: it applies whatever size
MiSTer_fb's reg has and with or without the RT series' ramoops node.

Evidence for every address, trigger type and exclusion, and how userspace
maps each node: docs/dts-mister-fpga-interface.md (Buildroot_MiSTer).

Provenance
----------
Origin:       None; authored for this tree. Folds in 0043 (2026-08-08) and
              0044 (2026-08-14), same author.
Author:       Michael C. Ferguson, 2026-11-13.
Upstream:     For the MiSTer kernel fork (export via
              scripts/export-kernel-tree.sh). generic-uio is bound through
              uio_pdrv_genirq.of_id; not a mainline binding.
Depends on:   0004 (the DTS base). 0045 makes mister,map-writecombine
              effective; without it the aperture maps strongly ordered.
              Needs CONFIG_UIO=y, CONFIG_UIO_PDRV_GENIRQ=y and
              uio_pdrv_genirq.of_id=generic-uio (linux.config).

Signed-off-by: Michael C. Ferguson <michael.christopher.ferguson@gmail.com>
---
